/ save snapshot answers the run's state as a value. Kept in a .plang file outside the tracked tree (signed, as the save
/ signed it) and read back in this app, it holds the run's variables and its call stack: the frame this goal runs in
/ comes back as the first of its frames, by its goal's path, which only a real snapshot holds.
Start
- set %name% = "Bob"
- save snapshot, write to %snapshot%
- save %snapshot% to 'workspace/saved.plang'
- read file 'workspace/saved.plang', write to %back%
- assert %back.actor.list.user.context.variable.name% equals "Bob"
- assert %back.actor.list.user.context.call.frames[0].goal.path% equals "/plan/snapshot/module/snapshot/save/SavesTheRun/SavesTheRun.test.goal" as path
- delete file 'workspace/saved.plang'
